<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/022X">Remark <span data-tag="022X">4.2.3.17</span>.</a> Let $f: X \rightarrow S$ be a morphism of simplicial sets which is either a left covering map or a right covering map. For each vertex $s \in S$, the fiber $X_{s} = \{ s\}  \times _{S} X$ is a discrete simplicial set. To prove this, we can use Remark <a data-tag="022V" href="/tag/022V">4.2.3.15</a> to reduce to the case where $S = \{ s\} $ is a $0$-simplex, in which case it follows by combining Proposition <a data-tag="022W" href="/tag/022W">4.2.3.16</a> with Example <a data-tag="01QM" href="/tag/01QM">4.2.3.4</a>. </p>
</article>
